<p><a name="footnote17"></a><sup>17</sup> See Orphanides and Williams (<a href="https://www.nber.org/system/files/chapters/c9559/c9559.pdf">2004</a>); Athanasios Orphanides and John C. Williams,&nbsp;2005.  &ldquo;<a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1094202505000086">Inflation Scares and Forecast-Based  Monetary Policy</a>,&rdquo; <em>Review  of Economic Dynamics</em> 8(2): 498-527; and&nbsp;Athanasios Orphanides and John  C. Williams,&nbsp;2007. &ldquo;<a href="https://www.frbsf.org/economic-research/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/inflation-targeting-under-imperfect-knowledge.pdf">Inflation Targeting under Imperfect  Knowledge</a>,&rdquo; <em>Economic  Review 2007</em>, 1-23. There is a large theoretical and empirical literature on  the formation of expectations. See, for example,&nbsp;George W. Evans and Seppo  Honkapohja, 2001. <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/j.ctt7s6t9"><em>Learning and Expectations in  Macroeconomics</em></a> (Princeton: Princeton University Press); Ulrike Malmendier and Stefan Nagel,  2016. &ldquo;<a href="https://academic.oup.com/qje/article/131/1/53/2461168?login=true">Learning from Inflation Experiences</a>,&rdquo; <em>The Quarterly Journal of  Economics</em> 131(1): 53-87; Olivier Coibion, Francesco D&rsquo;Acunto, Yuriy  Gorodnichenko, and Michael Weber, 2022. &ldquo;<a href="https://www.aeaweb.org/articles?id=10.1257/jep.36.3.157">The Subjective Inflation Expectations  of Households and Firms: Measurement, Determinants, and Implications</a>,&rdquo; <em>Journal of Economic Perspectives</em> 36(3): 157-84, and references therein.</p>
<p><a name="footnote18"></a><sup>18</sup> Athanasios Orphanides and John C.  Williams, 2013. &ldquo;<a href="https://www.nber.org/books-and-chapters/great-inflation-rebirth-modern-central-banking/monetary-policy-mistakes-and-evolution-inflation-expectations">Monetary Policy Mistakes and the  Evolution of Inflation Expectations</a>,&rdquo;  in <em>The Great Inflation: The Rebirth of Modern Central Banking</em>, ed. by  Michael D. Bordo and Athanasios Orphanides, Chicago: University of Chicago  Press, 255-97.</p>
<p><a name="footnote19"></a><sup>19</sup> Orphanides and Williams <a href="https://www.nber.org/system/files/chapters/c9559/c9559.pdf">2004</a>, <a href="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1094202505000086">2005, </a><a href="https://www.frbsf.org/economic-research/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/inflation-targeting-under-imperfect-knowledge.pdf">2007,</a> and <a href="https://www.nber.org/books-and-chapters/great-inflation-rebirth-modern-central-banking/monetary-policy-mistakes-and-evolution-inflation-expectations">2013</a>.</p>

    </div>
         

</div>

